.\" Man page for the XISOSharp CLI.
.\" Keep the flag set in sync with XISOSharp.Cli; scripts/check_cli_completions.py
.\" checks that every flag is present in all completion files.
.TH XISOSHARP 1 "2026-11-07" "XISOSharp 1.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xisosharp \- create, extract, list, rewrite and archive Xbox XISO/XDVDFS disc images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B XISOSharp
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-x\fR] \fIfile1.iso\fR [\fIfile2.iso\fR ...]
.br
.B XISOSharp
[\fIoptions\fR] \fB\-c\fR \fIdirectory\fR [\fIname\fR] ...
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBvalidate\fR \fIsource\fR \fIoutput\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBrebuild\fR \fIsource\fR [\fIvideo.iso\fR] [\fIfiller\fR|\fIseed\fR] [\fIsu20076000_00000000\fR] \fB\-o\fR \fIredump.iso\fR
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBbuild-image\fR [\fIsourceDir\fR] [\fIoutput.iso\fR] \fB\-m\fR \fIhost:image\fR [\fB\-f\fR \fItoml\fR] [\fB\-O\fR \fIoutput\fR] [\fB\-D\fR]
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBimage-spec\fR \fBfrom\fR \fB\-O\fR \fIout\fR \fB\-m\fR \fIhost:image\fR ... [\fIspecPath\fR]
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBcompress\fR|\fBcso\fR|\fBcci\fR \fIsource\fR [\fIoutput\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBdecompress\fR|\fBuncso\fR|\fBdecso\fR|\fBuncci\fR \fIcontainer\fR [\fIoutput.iso\fR]
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBchecksum\fR [\fB\-\-silent\fR] \fIimage\fR [\fIimages\fR ...]
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBhash\fR \fIimage\fR [\fIimages\fR ...] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBverify-hashes\fR \fIimage\fR \fIhash-file\fR [\fB\-\-ignore-extra\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBverify-dat\fR \fIdat\fR \fIimage\fR [\fIimages\fR ...] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBtitle-info\fR \fIimage\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBxbe-image\fR \fIimage\fR \fIpath\fR \fB\-\-type\fR \fIlogo\fR|\fItitle\fR|\fIsave\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIout.png\fR
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBsplit\fR [\fB\-\-size\fR \fIbytes\fR|\fIhalf\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIbase\fR] \fIimage\fR ...
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBjoin\fR [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIfile\fR] \fIfirst.1.iso\fR [...]
.br
.B XISOSharp
\fBconvert\fR \fIsource\fR \fIoutput\fR [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-n\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B XISOSharp
is a pure managed .NET tool for Xbox disc images. It is a port of
.BR extract-xiso (1)
with the archival modes of XboxKit and the packing/compression modes of
xdvdfs. One detection layer reads plain ISO, split \fI.1.iso\fR sets, CISO
(v1/v2), CCI/CCIM, ZAR, GOD/SVOD containers and read-only XBLA/XBLIG STFS
packages; the writer creates XISO images, CISO, CCI, ZAR and split sets.
.PP
With no mode flag the default is extract. Flags must precede positional
arguments; a flag after the first image name is refused. Read-only verbs
accept \fB\-\-json\fR, which writes machine-readable output to stdout and
human-readable logs to stderr.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B \-c \fIdirectory\fR [\fIname\fR]
Create an ISO from a directory. The optional \fIname\fR overrides the output
file name (default: the directory leaf name plus \fI.iso\fR). Repeatable for
batch creation.
.TP
.B \-\-pack \fIinput\fR [\fIname\fR]
Pack a directory into an ISO, or repack an existing ISO in place.
.TP
.B \-x
Extract (the default mode).
.TP
.B \-\-unpack \fIfile\fR [\fIdest\fR]
Unpack the whole image to \fIdest\fR (default: a directory named after the
image) and detect the optimized layout automatically.
.TP
.B \-l
List the top-level entries.
.TP
.B \-t
Recursively list the image tree.
.TP
.B \-i \fIfile\fR [\fIpath\fR]
Show volume descriptor metadata and per-entry details.
.TP
.B \-\-ls \fIfile\fR [\fIpath\fR]
List the names in one directory without recursion.
.TP
.B \-V \fIfile\fR ...
Audit one or more images (header, tree, sector bounds, cycles) or STFS
packages (SHA-1 hash tree).
.TP
.B \-r
Rewrite each ISO as an optimized ISO. The output is byte-identical to
.BR "extract-xiso \-r" .
.TP
.B \-\-repair \fIfile\fR
Fix safely patchable audit issues in place (reserved attribute bits, a
missing optimized tag, separators in names).
.TP
.B \-\-salvage \fIfile\fR
Rebuild a readable image from a corrupt one, dropping unreadable entries.
.TP
.B validate \fIsource\fR \fIoutput\fR
Compare the file trees of two images. Both sides accept ISO, CISO, CCI, split
sets, GOD and ZAR.
.TP
.B rebuild \fIsource\fR [\fIvideo.iso\fR] [\fIfiller\fR|\fIseed\fR] [\fIsu...\fR] \fB\-o\fR \fIredump.iso\fR
Rebuild a Redump-style ISO from an extracted XISO and its parts.
.TP
.B build-image [\fIsourceDir\fR] [\fIoutput.iso\fR] \fB\-m\fR \fIhost:image\fR
Build an image from ordered \fBwax\fR remap rules; reads a
\fIxdvdfs.toml\fR with \fB\-f\fR and previews with \fB\-D\fR.
.TP
.B image-spec from \fB\-O\fR \fIout\fR \fB\-m\fR \fIhost:image\fR ...
Generate an xdvdfs TOML spec from map rules.
.TP
.B compress\fR|\fBcso\fR|\fBcci\fR \fIsource\fR [\fIoutput\fR]
Compress to CISO or CCI. Use \fB\-\-format\fR to choose the container.
.TP
.B decompress\fR|\fBuncso\fR|\fBdecso\fR|\fBuncci\fR \fIcontainer\fR [\fIoutput.iso\fR]
Decompress CISO, CCI or a GOD container to a plain ISO.
.TP
.B checksum [\fB\-\-silent\fR] \fIimage\fR ...
Compute the SHA3-256 tree checksum (xdvdfs compatible). ISO, split ISO,
CISO, CCI, GOD, ZAR and STFS inputs compare equally when their trees match.
.TP
.B hash \fIimage\fR ...
Compute CRC32, MD5, SHA-1, SHA-256 and SHA3-256 in one pass.
.TP
.B verify-hashes \fIimage\fR \fIhash-file\fR
Verify a \fI*.hash\fR sidecar produced by \fB\-\-petrify\fR.
.TP
.B verify-dat \fIdat\fR \fIimage\fR ...
Match whole images against a Redump-style XML DAT by size and MD5/SHA-1/CRC32;
report verified, ambiguous, not-in-DAT and missing entries.
.TP
.B title-info \fIimage\fR
Show title metadata from XBE/XEX, XDBF/XSRC or GOD/STFS XContent headers.
.TP
.B xbe-image \fIimage\fR \fIpath\fR \fB\-\-type\fR \fIlogo|title|save\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIout\fR
Extract the Microsoft logo, title image or save image as PNG or DDS.
.TP
.B split [\fB\-\-size\fR \fIbytes\fR|\fIhalf\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIbase\fR] \fIimage\fR ...
Split a plain ISO into sector-aligned parts.
.TP
.B join [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIfile\fR] \fIfirst.1.iso\fR ...
Reassemble split parts and validate the result.
.TP
.B convert \fIsource\fR \fIoutput\fR
Convert between ISO and ZAR, or decompress a GOD container to ISO/CISO/CCI.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.B \-d \fIdirectory\fR
Extract destination directory, or the rewrite output directory.
.TP
.B \-D
Delete the \fI.old\fR source after a successful rewrite. As
\fBbuild-image \-D\fR, preview the host-to-image mapping without writing.
.TP
.B \-o \fIfilename\fR
Output file name for rewrite, rebuild and compression modes.
.TP
.B \-O \fIfilename\fR
Output file name for \fBbuild-image\fR and \fBimage-spec\fR.
.TP
.B \-m
Create/rewrite: disable the automatic XBE media-enable patch. In
\fBbuild-image\fR, supply a \fIhost:image\fR map rule.
.TP
.B \-f \fItoml\fR
Read \fIxdvdfs.toml\fR map rules for \fBbuild-image\fR.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet: suppress non-error output.
.TP
.B \-Q
Silent: suppress all output, including errors.
.TP
.B \-s
Skip \fI$SystemUpdate\fR entries.
.TP
.B \-X \fIglob\fR
Create mode: exclude files or directories matching the pattern. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Overwrite outputs without prompting.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-no
Never overwrite; refuse when an output exists.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print the version banner plus component, runtime and commit details.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage and exit 0.
.SS Extraction and reading
.TP
.B \-\-skip-sectors \fIN\fR
Treat the XISO filesystem as starting \fIN\fR sectors into the file (Redump
images with a video partition).
.TP
.B \-\-skip-existing
Skip files that already exist with matching sizes (resume an interrupted
unpack).
.TP
.B \-\-continue-on-error
Log per-file extraction failures and continue; the run still exits non-zero.
.TP
.B \-\-name-policy \fIreject\fR|\fIsanitize\fR|\fIskip\fR
How to handle host-unsafe entry names during extraction.
.TP
.B \-\-copy-out \fIiso\fR \fIpath\fR \fIdest\fR
Copy a file or directory out of an image.
.TP
.B \-\-copy-in \fIiso\fR \fIhost\fR \fIpath\fR
Copy a host file into an image in place.
.TP
.B \-\-no-backup
Skip the \fI.old\fR backup for \fB\-\-copy-in\fR and \fB\-\-repair\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-md5 \fIiso\fR [\fIpath\fR]
Compute MD5 hashes of files inside the image.
.TP
.B \-\-sha256 \fIiso\fR [\fIpath\fR]
Compute SHA-256 hashes of files inside the image.
.TP
.B \-\-xex-info \fIiso\fR \fIpath\fR
Show the Xbox 360 XEX2 header and XDBF/XSRC metadata.
.TP
.B \-\-xbe-info \fIiso\fR \fIpath\fR
Show the original-Xbox XBEH header and certificate.
.TP
.B \-\-filetime \fIiso\fR
Show the volume descriptor FILETIME.
.TP
.B \-\-get-filetime \fIiso\fR
Alias of \fB\-\-filetime\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-set-filetime \fIiso\fR \fIvalue\fR
Set the volume descriptor FILETIME.
.TP
.B \-\-sector-layout \fIiso\fR
Print the full on-disk sector map.
.TP
.B \-\-ranges \fIiso\fR
Print the system and file sector ranges.
.TP
.B \-\-is-optimized \fIiso\fR
Report whether the optimized tag is present.
.SS Writing and containers
.TP
.B \-\-prepend-sectors \fIN\fR
Write \fIN\fR empty sectors before the XISO filesystem (video-partition room).
.TP
.B \-\-layout \fIfile\fR
Pack entries at the sectors named by a sector-layout JSON/text file.
.TP
.B \-\-preserve-attrs
Rewrite mode: keep the source dirent attribute bits instead of the
extract-xiso parity defaults.
.TP
.B \-\-file-time \fIvalue\fR
Fixed FILETIME for create, pack and build-image (ISO-8601, raw, hex,
\fInow\fR or \fI0\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-jobs \fIN\fR
Parallel workers (1\-64) for extraction, CISO/CCI compression, batch
conversion, ZAR creation and multi-image checksum/hash/audit/list/tree/rewrite.
Output is byte-identical to \fB\-\-jobs 1\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-symlink-mode \fIfollow|skip|reject\fR
Create-time link policy for \fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-pack\fR, \fBbuild-image\fR and
\fBapply-skeleton\fR. \fIfollow\fR packs file links as target content and skips
directory reparse points; \fIskip\fR omits both; \fIreject\fR fails with the
link path.
.TP
.B \-\-batch \fIdirectory\fR
Process every supported image in a directory.
.TP
.B \-\-batch-recursive
Search subdirectories for \fB\-\-batch\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-output-name \fItemplate\fR
Name batch outputs from \fI{name}\fR, \fI{ext}\fR and \fI{format}\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-delete-source
Delete each source after a successful batch conversion (requires
\fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIcso\fR|\fIcci\fR|\fIiso\fR|\fIzar\fR
Container format for \fBcompress\fR and \fBconvert --batch\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-ciso-level \fI0..9\fR
CISO compression level (default 9).
.TP
.B \-\-ciso-version \fI1\fR|\fI2\fR|\fIauto\fR
CISO format version.
.TP
.B \-\-ciso-split \fIbytes\fR
Split CISO output at the given size (0 writes a single file).
.TP
.B \-\-cci-level \fI0..12\fR
CCI compression level; 10\-12 select the LZ4-HC encoder.
.TP
.B \-\-cci-split \fIbytes\fR
Split CCI output at the given size.
.TP
.B \-\-size \fIbytes\fR|\fIhalf\fR
Split size for \fBsplit\fR; \fIhalf\fR splits in two.
.TP
.B \-\-policy \fIskip\fR|\fIoverwrite\fR|\fIauto-rename\fR
Overwrite policy for ZAR creation without prompting.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore-extra
\fBverify-hashes\fR: ignore files present in the image but absent from the
sidecar.
.SS Redump archival
.TP
.B \-\-video
Extract the video partition.
.TP
.B \-\-random
Extract random filler/padding.
.TP
.B \-\-seed
Extract the XGD1 RNG seed.
.TP
.B \-\-wipe
Zero filler gaps.
.TP
.B \-\-trim
Truncate after the last file extent.
.TP
.B \-\-petrify
Write a skeleton image plus a SHA-1 \fI.hash\fR sidecar.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Extract the system update \fIsu20076000_00000000\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-zar
Write a ZArchive (\fI.zar\fR) alongside the image.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Alias: \fB\-\-random \-\-seed \-\-trim \-\-update \-\-video \-\-wipe\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-best
Alias: \fB\-\-trim \-\-wipe\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-compress
Alias: \fB\-\-petrify \-\-update \-\-video \-\-zar\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-security-sectors \fIfile\fR
Rebuild only: override the security-sector ranges from a \fIstart-end\fR file.
.TP
.B \-\-sectors \fIfile\fR
Alias of \fB\-\-security-sectors\fR.
.SS Output and validation
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output for read-only modes.
.TP
.B \-\-silent
Checksum: print only the hash.
.TP
.B \-\-validate, \-\-validate-strict, \-\-validate-checksums, \-\-validate-report
Validation flavors; \fB\-V\fR is the audit form.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
With \fB\-\-repair\fR, preview fixes without changing the file.
.TP
.B \-\-repair-out \fIpath\fR
With \fB\-\-salvage\fR, choose the rebuilt image path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, unreadable/corrupt input, failed validation/audit, or a failed
operation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XISO_NO_UPDATE_CHECK
Disable the daily GitHub release check performed by the CLI and GUI.
.TP
.B XISO_NO_PAUSE
Never wait for a keypress after a double-click launch.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I *.iso
Plain or optimized XISO image.
.TP
.I *.1.iso, *.2.iso, ...
Split plain ISO set.
.TP
.I *.cso, *.1.cso, ...
CISO container (v1 or v2), optionally split.
.TP
.I *.cci, *.1.cci, ...
CCI/CCIM container, optionally split.
.TP
.I *.zar
ZArchive (zstd) archive.
.TP
.I *.hash
SHA-1 sidecar written by \fB\-\-petrify\fR or verified by \fBverify-hashes\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
Extract an image into a directory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
XISOSharp \-x game.iso \-d out
.RE
.fi
.PP
List an image as JSON:
.PP
.nf
.RS
XISOSharp \-l game.iso \-\-json
.RE
.fi
.PP
Create a deterministic ISO from a folder:
.PP
.nf
.RS
XISOSharp \-c src game.iso \-\-file-time 0
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compress to a split CCI with parallel workers:
.PP
.nf
.RS
XISOSharp compress game.iso game.cci \-\-format cci \-\-jobs 8
.RE
.fi
.PP
Verify two images have the same file tree:
.PP
.nf
.RS
XISOSharp validate game.iso game.1.cso
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR extract-xiso (1),
.BR xdvdfs (1)
.PP
Full documentation: \fIhttps://purelogiccode.github.io/XISOSharp/\fR
